the machine, didn't know how to use a mill or a lathe or a high-speed, you know, metal band, so on. I'd never worked with anything that heavy before. I was completely inexperienced, you know, broke tools. I had to get more materials. And I had this idea in my head about this perfect wrench that I'd seen that was, you know, bought from a very expensive supplier. And then I finally realized what I was doing was, which is a metaphor for the rest of real life is, I'm trying to make a real thing. I'm trying to bring it into being. I'm trying to take something and allow something real, something finite, something limited, something constrained, something even with flaws in it, to come into being. And all that struggle with, you know, breaking parts and what have you,
这台机器，不知道怎么用铣床、车床或高速金属带锯等等。我以前从未处理过那么重的东西。我完全缺乏经验，你知道的，弄坏了工具。我不得不获取更多的材料。我脑子里有一个完美的扳手概念，那是我从一家非常昂贵的供应商那里看到的。然后我终于意识到我在做什么，这其实是现实生活中其他事情的一个隐喻：我正在试图制造一个真实的东西。我试图把它带入现实。我试图拿一样东西，让某种真实的东西、某种有限的、有约束力的、甚至带有瑕疵的东西变为现实。所有那些与弄坏零件等情况的斗争，

